&P338788 = ARM 04, 026 
#atf: lang akk 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. [a]-na ia-as2-ma-ah-{d}[iszkur] 
#tr.ts: ana yasmaḫ-addu 
#tr.en: To Yasmaḫ-Addu 
2. qi2#-bi2-[ma] 
#tr.ts: qibima 
#tr.en: speak! 
3. um-ma isz-me-{d}da-gan a-hu-ka-a-ma 
#tr.ts: umma išme-dagan aḫukama 
#tr.en: Thus Išme-Dagan, your brother: 
4. ki-ma qa-du-um s,a#-bi#-im a-na ne2-e'2-ra-ri-im 
#tr.ts: kīma qadum ṣābim ana ne’rārim 
#tr.en: Since with the troops to aid 
5. a-na re-esz sa-mu-{d}iszkur ku-ul-lim 
#tr.ts: ana reš samu-addu kullim 
#tr.en: and support Samu-Addu 
6. a-na ka-ra-na-a{ki} al-li-kam 
#tr.ts: ana karanaya allikam 
#tr.en: to Karanaya I went, 
7. wu-di i-na pa-ni-tim-ma 
#tr.ts: wuddi ina panītimma 
#tr.en: certainly earlier 
8. asz-pu-ra-kum 
#tr.ts: ašpurakkum 
#tr.en: I wrote to you; 
9. _lu2_ esz3-nun-na{ki} qa-du-um ga-ma-ar-ti s,a-bi-szu 
#tr.ts: awīl ešnunna qadum gamarti ṣābišu
#tr.en: the man of Ešnunna with the ensemble of his troops,
10. qa-du-um _giri3-se3-ga-mesz_ 
#tr.ts: qadum girseqqî 
#tr.en: together with administrative staff 
11. u3 be-el du-um-qi2 
#tr.ts: u bēl dumqī 
#tr.en: and notables, 
12. ip#-hu-ur-ma i-na u2-pe2{ki} 
#tr.ts: ipḫurma ina upe 
#tr.en: gathered, and in Opis
13. [wa]-szi-ib-ma 
#tr.ts: wašibma 
#tr.en: sat, and 
14. [u3 a-na] _lu2_ babila{ki} 
#tr.ts: u ana awīl bābilim 
#tr.en: further to the man of Babylon 
15. [a-na it]-ti-szu ne-en-mu-di-im 
#tr.ts: ana ittišu nenmudim 
#tr.en: to meet up with him 
16. [i-na ma]-an-ki-si{ki} 
#tr.ts: ina mankisi 
#tr.en: in Mankisi 
17. [...]-x-e-em 
#tr.ts: ...-em 
#tr.en: ... 
@reverse 
1. isz#-ta-ap-pa-ar-ma 
#tr.ts: ištapparma 
#tr.en: kept writing, but  
